(2a) exact low levels: E_1 = 2/3 (err 1.1e-16), E_2 = 10/21 (err 1.1e-16); ||pi||_2^2 = 15/7.
     L^2 mass on classes 1 and 2 mod 3 is exactly 1/5 : 4/5 at every level (|kappa_+^|^2 : |kappa_-^|^2 = 1 : 4 pointwise).
     max_y pi(y + 3^n Z_3) = pi(-1 + 3^n Z_3) ~ c 2^-n: the L^infinity dimension is log_3 2 = 0.631 > 1/2.
     level energies E_n rise slowly towards ~0.476 (increments shrink like ~1/n or faster);  ||pi||_n^2 ~ 0.47 n.
     L^1 increments ||p_n - p_{n-1}||_1 shrink slowly (last ratio 0.928); consistent with L^1 convergence (absolute continuity of pi), not a proof.

