(2c) ladder autocorrelations C_j^(n) = 3^n sum_y pi_n(y) pi_n(S^j y), S(y) = 4y+1 (translation by j in the
     coordinates Lambda = log_4(1+3y)), and the identity ||pi||_{n+1}^2 = sum_j 4^-|j| C_j^(n):
   n=14: C_1..C_12 = 0.7281 0.4733 1.2370 0.8604 0.7650 1.3716 0.4278 0.7506 2.1116 0.5210 0.5917 1.5276
   C_27 = 2.3616 (v_3 = 3),  C_9 = 2.1116 (v_3 = 2),  C_3 = 1.2370 (v_3 = 1): C_j grows with v_3(j) (log singularity at 0).
   sum_j 4^-|j| C_j^(14) = 8.213596069255   vs   ||pi||_15^2 = 8.213596069255   (difference 1.6e-14; tail |j|>40 < 1e-23)
   so E_{n+1} = 2 sum_{j>=1} 4^-j C_j^(n): the level energy is bounded iff the off-diagonal ladder correlations are.

