====================================================================================================
PART 5. Mean-field smoothing transform vs the exact 3-adic cascade; moment functions; strips
====================================================================================================
(5a) g_q(s) = 2^-s (1 + q^(s-1)) = E_fwd[w^(s-1)], w in {1/2, q/2} with probability 1/2 each:
     g_q(1) = 1 (mean), g_q(2) = (1+q)/4 = AM of the forward factors, -g_q'(1) = -E log w = log(2/sqrt q) (> 0: contracting):
   q   g_q(2)    -g_q'(1) = log(4/q)/2   roots of g_q(s) = 1
   1   0.5000    0.693147                 {1}
   3   1.0000    0.143841                 {1, 2}
   5   1.5000    -0.111572                {0.6509, 1}
   7   2.0000    -0.279808                {0.3735, 1}
   9   2.5000    -0.405465                {0.2581, 1}
   q = 3 is the only q with g_q(2) = 1: this is THM-4470's AM-fairness (q+1)/4 = 1, and makes kappa = 2.
   q = 3: -g'(1) = log(2/sqrt 3) = 0.143841 (the drift), tree-density constant R = 1/log(2/sqrt 3) = 6.95212 (inverse-tree note, Prop. 10);
          g'(2) = ln(27/16)/4 = 0.130812 > 0 (Kesten-Goldie-type slope at kappa = 2); the s=2 tilt has odd-step frequency 3/4.

(5b) Zolotarev zeta_s contraction constants of the mean-field smoothing transform S: zeta_s(S mu, S nu) <= g(s) zeta_s(mu, nu)
     (ideal metric of order s, 1 < s <= 2, laws with equal means):
     s:    1.100   1.250   1.500   1.750   1.900   2.000 
     g(s): 0.9872  0.9738  0.9659  0.9750  0.9881  1.0000
     strict contraction exactly on 1 < s < 2; the constant is 1 at s = 2: the Banach fixed-point argument and the
     Cauchy-Schwarz lower bound fail at the same place, g(2) = 1.

(5c) mean-field cascade: E[Z_k^2] = 1 + k/2 exactly (siblings independent); exact 3-adic values are smaller:
